{"componentChunkName":"component---src-templates-news-detail-template-js","path":"/blog/all-about-uae-public-holidays-2024/","result":{"data":{"strapiBlog":{"createdAt":"2023-12-14T08:51:19.910Z","updatedAt":"2024-11-18T03:53:18.452Z","video_url":null,"title":"All About UAE Public Holidays 2024","short_description":"Planning for the upcoming public holidays in the UAE for 2024? Find out when private and public institutions will be closed. Thanks to the Cabinet's early announcement, residents of the UAE can plan their vacations, coordinate travel arrangements, and schedule other family activities well in advance. Take a look at the comprehensive list of UAE public holidays for 2024.","tile_image":{"url":"https://ggfx-providentestate.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/i/mercer_feature_d44fbc6a0e.jpg"},"team_contact":null,"strapi_id":123,"slug":"all-about-uae-public-holidays-2024","publish":true,"id":"74c1904d-ef48-541f-8ee4-73a49503dadb","rank":null,"date":"December 14, 2023","category":{"strapi_json_value":[],"id":"f69d3548-8fa3-55a4-9939-7ad1b0ae4327"},"banner_image":{"url":"https://ggfx-providentestate.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/i/blog_0442c7ee24.jpg"},"author":null,"modules":[{"id":"1158a8f6-2f2a-5ef1-a7e0-05ac04f5a319","strapi_component":"components.rich-text-block","strapi_id":238,"text":{"data":{"text":"<p>Planning for the upcoming public holidays in the UAE for 2024? Find out when private and public institutions will be closed. Thanks to the Cabinet's early announcement, residents of the UAE can plan their vacations, coordinate travel arrangements, and schedule other family activities well in advance. Take a look at the comprehensive list of UAE public holidays for 2024.</p><h3>Official Public Holidays UAE 2024</h3><p>The residents can enjoy many official holidays next year, from religious festivals to personal celebrations. Religious observances, such as Eid al-Fitr and Eid al-Adha, are a great time to understand their cultural importance and the shared joy they bring to communities across the UAE.&nbsp;</p><p>Similarly, UAE National Day is the perfect time to celebrate the spirit of unity and patriotism. Uncover the historical narratives and traditions that bind the people, fostering a sense of pride and belonging. Here is a list of the confirmed UAE holidays in 2024:</p><figure class=\"table\" style=\"width:100%;\"><table class=\"ck-table-resized\"><colgroup><col style=\"width:50%;\"><col style=\"width:50%;\"></colgroup><tbody><tr><td><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;\">New Year’s Day</span></p></td><td><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;\">Monday, 1st January</span></p></td></tr><tr><td><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;\">Eid al Fitr 2024 UAE</span></p></td><td><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;\">29 Ramadan – 3 Shawwal</span></p></td></tr><tr><td><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;\">Arafat Day</span></p></td><td><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;\">9 Dhul Hijjah</span></p></td></tr><tr><td><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;\">Eid Al-Adha</span></p></td><td><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;\">10 to 12 Dhul Hijjah</span></p></td></tr><tr><td><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;\">Islamic New Year</span></p></td><td><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;\">1 Muharram</span></p></td></tr><tr><td><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;\">Prophet Muhammad’s (PBUH) birthday</span></p></td><td><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;\">12 Rabi’ Al-Awwal</span></p></td></tr><tr><td><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;\">National Day</span></p></td><td><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap;\">Monday, 2nd and Tuesday, 3rd December</span></p></td></tr></tbody></table></figure><h3>How Many Public Holidays Are There in the UAE?</h3><p>In 2024, the UAE is slated to observe a minimum of 13 public holidays, and notably, four of the seven official occasions will result in extended weekends.</p><style>.ck-table-resized{border-collapse:collapse;}.ck-table-resized td{border: 1px solid black;}</style>"}}},{"id":"b03b7bc1-ca90-5103-bcb0-b9f7e911471c","strapi_id":136,"strapi_component":"modules.ads-banner","small":false,"marketing_banner":{"title":"Our Expert Advisors Tailor Loans to Your Needs","bg_image":{"url":"https://ggfx-providentestate.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/i/mortgage_experts_d74dcf3a44.jpg"},"icon":null,"cta":{"cta_label":"Contact Us","custom_link":null,"isExternal":false,"icon":null,"id":"f4b49cbf-a341-59cf-b0e4-ba312c54d052","strapi_id":760,"menu":{"title":"General Enquiry","page":{"layout":"form_page","id":"4c8cd67e-65fc-5e12-bb3c-6c1e48adb07c","publish":true,"page_name":"General Enquiry","strapi_id":57},"strapi_parent":{"slug":"contact","title":"Contact","publish":true,"link_type":"internal","id":33},"link_type":"internal","slug":"general-enquiry","strapi_id":66,"id":"fac7c4b3-a6f1-55e9-ada7-8466e85fe1d2"}},"cta1":null,"description":{"data":{"description":"<p>Start Your Homeownership Journey Today.</p>"}},"ggfx_results":[{"src_cftle":"i/mortgage_experts_d74dcf3a44.jpg","transforms":[{"url":"https://ggfx-providentestate.s3.eu-west-2.amazonaws.com/x/492x/mortgage_exper